            <ArticleTitle>Effect of ignoring genotype-environment interaction on segregation analysis of quantitative traits.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>581-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty replicates of 200 nuclear families (6 members each) were generated under three GxE interaction models. Segregation analyses of these data were performed using a regressive model taking into account an interaction effect or not. Results showed that ignoring the GxE interaction markedly decreased the power for accepting a major gene and led to serious bias in parameter estimates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
